25,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The late-turn pool is dangerously thin, but the lift maintenance contract actually has spare capacity.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The old accessibility work was mixed; lifts did well, but lane-priority failed. Also, a late-evening pilot actually worked.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Pre-war shells are risky due to unrecorded voids. Also, ferry and rail back offices can't agree on data terms.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The capital ledger has a ring-fenced construction balance, but the technology line was trimmed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Mid-city runs are slower, but crowds clear at the same rate. Most delays are actually waiting for connections.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Takumi, if the late-evening pilot worked, do we have the staff to repeat it now?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"I only know it worked then, not if we have the people now.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, you mentioned the late-turn pool is thin. That sounds like a problem for night services.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,The ticketing fees are higher than the paving budget... that seems wrong.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"If the delays are in the connections, maybe we don't need more buses mid-city?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Victoria,,Exactly. Overtime is already covering everything. A night extension would be a nightmare for the current crew.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, if the pre-war shells are a gamble, then station upgrades might be too risky.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Agreed. The voids make the timeline unpredictable.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, if the technology budget is trimmed, can we even afford a new fare platform?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I didn't think about the budget! I just thought about the passengers.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Victoria,,We should avoid anything that strains the rosters or relies on unstable data agreements.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Takumi,,The lane-priority failures from before make me wary of the bus corridor too.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"The roadway consents are already delegated, though. That's a plus for the corridor.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm worried about the long-term costs of these contracts.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Sakura,,Maybe the station upgrades are best since the maintenance crew is ready?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
