50,3,1,talk,Victoria,,Candidate B is out because of the rosters. Candidate D is risky due to the data terms Toshio found.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Candidate A has a history of failing in this city. I'm leaning toward C.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Candidate C has the ""void"" risk, but the maintenance capacity is a strong offset.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Candidate C uses the construction balance, which is ring-fenced. That's safer for the budget.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Sakura,,I like C! It fixes the stations and we have the people to maintain them.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Victoria,,I agree. C is the most sustainable option for the staff.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Takumi,,It's better than repeating the mistakes of the bus lanes.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Toshio,,It's the most logical choice given the constraints.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I feel comfortable with C.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Sakura,,Yay! Everyone agrees!,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
